WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.430 align:start position:0%
 
who are these people  they're you  they're me  they're european citizens  they came to strasbourg this morning to  make their voices heard on the future of  europe on the european union they want  to build  many of them are young people  and the future is in their hands  they have seized the opportunities set  out by the president of the european  commission ursula van der leyen who  called for a new push for european  democracy when she took office  the european parliament the council of  the european union and the european  commission jointly agreed to put  participatory democracy front and center  the conference on the future of europe  was born  against a tense international backdrop  with the kovid 19 pandemic and now the  war in ukraine  europeans must stick together  they must renew the dialogue with the  politicians who represent them  they must review their collective  priorities in every domain  without taboos  getting involved means helping to shape  the future of eu policies  we have to strengthen the role of our  role and we have to sit at the table  when big decisions are being brought  there is no time to lose  the world of tomorrow is a world of  empires it's a world of danger  we have seen it with ukraine  and in this world we need  to defend ourselves to organize  ourselves  [Music]  in march 2021 the european parliament  the portuguese presidency of the council  of the european union and the european  commission signed a joint declaration on  how this new space for debate with  citizens would be organized  a few days later an online platform in  24 languages was launched a place for  europeans to submit their ideas and  exchange in real time with fellow  citizens all over europe thanks to  electronic translation  a key tool for discovering about all  conference related events and above all  to define common expectations for what  the european union should be doing in  future  the conference on the future of europe  had officially begun  the conference is not a conference in  the classic sense of the word  it's a year-long democratic process at  all levels  individual and collective local regional  national  and european  the process indeed is based on three  main pillars and they are the most  innovative elements of the conference  the first pillar is the multilingual  digital platform  the second pillar of the conference  consists of 800 randomly selected  european citizens from across the 27  member states grouped into four european  panels of 200 citizens  these groups met several times online or  in person  in natalin florence dublin maastricht  and strasbourg between september 2021  and february 2022 their task to agree on  the recommendations they would like to  submit to the conference plenary  the conference plenary is the third  pillar  with about 450 members and the big  innovation  in this  plenary is the fact that we were mixing  political representatives with citizens  it gathers 108 citizens including 80  citizens acting as ambassadors for the  european citizens panels as well as 108  representatives of the national  parliaments 108 members of the european  parliament 54 council representatives or  two per member state and representatives  of the european commission and of  european consultative bodies organized  civil society and social partners  democracy  is very important uh part of our lives  so this conference is organized in order  to come closer to citizens and to fill  the gap which evidently exists between  policy makers and our citizens  three european commission vice  presidents were mobilized to respond  directly to citizens questions  dubravka schwitzer the co-chair of the  conference's executive board marash  chefchavich and vera eurova  each european citizens panel discussed  and debated in 24 languages key  priorities for european citizens  health climate change in the environment  migration education  jobs social justice or democracy itself  to name a few they have issued a series  of recommendations and in march and  april 2022 these recommendations were  presented in plenary in strasbourg and  turned into proposals proposals approved  in plenary taken together formed the  final report of the conference on the  future of europe they came with very  different views and very different ideas  but all of them came with a commitment  that really enriched the process  let's take a look at a few examples the  europeans working on the topics of a  stronger economy social justice and jobs  formulated concrete recommendations on  innovation the reinforcement of the  single market sustainable growth and the  demographic transition  meanwhile europeans focusing on  education culture youth and sport  proposed the creation of a european  education area with transnational  learning opportunities accessible to all  by 2025 as well as the reinforcement of  cultural exchanges  and together citizens looking into  issues related to the digital  transformation looked at ever more  pressing challenges like data protection  and the fight against disinformation  when we get to talk together on one  table on  different subjects we actually really  get to know each other it's a really  nice message that everyone is working  together in such a beautiful ways 27  states is not it's not easy to get to  work together topics as mental health  and sexual education are very important  to talk work it's not your life it's  only a part of it an amazing  demonstration of participatory democracy  and i think we should bring them into  the future more and more and get the  citizens involved  citizens who worked on european  democracy tackled big questions such as  how we could be more involved in the  preparation of european policies whilst  building closer links with our elected  representatives  they proposed regular citizens  assemblies  europe-wide referendums  the promotion of democratic civic  education and facilitating access to  information about the eu for everyone  europeans looking into climate change  and the environment didn't shy away from  ideas to save the planet touching on  topics as varied as food production  public transport and the crucial matter  of european energy supplies  and when it came to health participants  discussed mental health accessibility  and the price and quality of care for  everyone i get a better understanding of  how the eu works in general the people  are not here for the politicians  politicians are here for people  everybody can change the situation can  change the world it's important to to  make the citizens have a greater impact  on the decision making we didn't know  what was coming out of it but now we see  like the recommendations come to life  and that's really great one european  citizens panel explored the themes of  the eu's place in the world and  migration  they were united in their desire to see  europe reduce its dependence on industry  and energy from abroad and boost  cooperation on matters like defence and  diplomacy  and in terms of migration participants  put solidarity and the human dimension  first  they expressed support for efforts to  promote economic growth and opportunity  in so-called countries of origin  coupled with a truly common european  migration policy  we  want to make the life from migrants the  better we have to work hard and we have  to be better as a society as a union to  improve in total the conference on the  future of europe brought together more  than a million participants from across  the eu in some 6500 events national  citizens panels and european citizens  panels some eighteen thousand ideas  twenty two thousand comments seventy  three thousand endorsements from all  over europe fed into citizens  recommendations discussed in plenary in  strasbourg  there is a benchmark which is called  follow-up and feedback mechanism we are  gathering all their proposals and all  their recommendations we will cluster  them into the report  on the 9th of may 2022 the conference  draws to a close with the submission of  its proposals drawn from the citizens  recommendations into a final report to  the european parliament the council of  the european union and the european  commission but this isn't the end  it's the beginning of a new phase in the  policy-making process which reinforces  citizens voices at the heart of the  european union  it is only the beginning of our work if  you want to say something just say it  it's not about nations it's about europe  we all have to do it all together we are  strong democracy and what we have done  here will make us only stronger we are  the power  [Music]

